Zugg, or Zuggarian, is a merfolk wizard and a friend of [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]], who helped raise the citadel of [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]]. He is one of the three founders of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], alongside [[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]] and [[People/Rotok|Rotok]], and lives on immortally. He is powerful, very clever and paranoid, and the Broker keeps him as a method of last resort: the last time Zugg was brought into a recovery, close to a hundred thousand clones of him broke away, founded a country of their own and took the greater part of the continent they stood on. He is away raising a second citadel of his own.

Zugg was one of the party on [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] that killed [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]], and afterwards founded Sedecium with his friends' help, on the technology of a wrecked Sundom ship, the knowledge of [[Geography/Althane/The Archive|Archive]]'s library and what [[People/Althane/SeRaan|SeRaan]] knew of the worlds beyond. He offered [[People/Rotok|Rotok]] immortality, again and again.
